# @aster-cloud scope hosted on GitHub Packages.
#
# Auth: requires GITHUB_TOKEN (or NPM_TOKEN) env var with read:packages
# scope at install time.
#
# Local dev:
#   1. Create a Classic PAT at github.com/settings/tokens
#      → scopes: read:packages (write:packages only needed for publishing)
#   2. Add to shell: `export GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_xxx`
#   3. Run `pnpm install`
#
# CI (Cloudflare Workers build):
#   Pass via the build env vars. Pages/Workers UI → Settings → Environment
#   variables → add GITHUB_TOKEN (secret).
#
# Why GITHUB_TOKEN rather than NODE_AUTH_TOKEN: the variable name only
# matters at install time — `${GITHUB_TOKEN}` is conventional outside
# GitHub Actions and avoids confusing dev/CI cross-talk.
@aster-cloud:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${GITHUB_TOKEN}
always-auth=true
